10	# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012
11	
12	**Strategy**: Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs
13	**Triage**: Full decomposition (not below threshold, not docs-only). The strategy spans multiple components and teams (Platform Operator, Data Science Pipelines, model serving, Documentation), introduces a new platform component (a bundled S3-compatible store), and contains a genuine unknown (AGPL-3.0 redistribution clearance) whose outcome changes which upstream is productized.
14	
15	## Strategy Structure Notes
16	
17	- The strategy provides an HLR table and an Affected Components list, but **no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no NFR section** — recorded as health warnings below. Teams are inferred from architecture context owning teams and standard platform naming; epic acceptance criteria are derived from the HLRs.
18	- Affected Components lists Platform Operator, Data Science Pipelines, Dashboard, and Documentation. HLR-3 additionally names model serving, mapped to the canonical component **Serving Runtimes** (see Component Mappings).
19	- The bundled S3-compatible object store is a **new component**: it has no canonical RHAI Jira component and no architecture context file. Per the new-component rule, it gets the full onboarding chain (repo-onboarding + license-validation in parallel → konflux-onboarding → general implementation), gated on the legal investigation because the upstream identity (MinIO vs Apache-2.0 fallback) is undecided.
20	
21	## Component Mappings (non-obvious)
22	
23	| Strategy term | Canonical component | Rationale |
24	|---|---|---|
25	| Bundled S3-compatible object store (MinIO / SeaweedFS) | Platform Operator | No canonical storage component exists; the store is bundled and enabled through the Platform Operator, the closest parent-level component. Needs `epic-creator-needs-component` treatment. |
26	| Model serving (HLR-3) | Serving Runtimes | Closest canonical match for model serving connection defaults. |
27	| Dashboard | Dashboard | Listed as affected but no change is described; treated as **passive** (see below). |
28	
29	## Passive Component Handling
30	
31	- **Dashboard**: listed in Affected Components with no described change. The bundled store is administrator-facing infrastructure enabled through the Platform Operator; no Dashboard surface is specified in the strategy. Treated as passive — "keep working" validation becomes acceptance criteria on the consumer epics (Data Science Pipelines and Serving Runtimes defaults): pipeline runs and model serving views must continue to function in the Dashboard when connections target the bundled store. Flagged as a health warning for human verification, since the Dashboard architecture context notes that user-facing enablement of a component normally requires a Dashboard integration.
